     5	#
     6	# WHY THIS EXISTS (v1.3.0-rc.1 re-pass, F2 + the F1/F2 composite risk):
     7	#
     8	#   (a) ANCESTRY. Nothing verified that the commit being tagged is on main.
     9	#       `bump` could create a local commit AFTER the preflight proved CI green
    10	#       for a different SHA, and `tag()` would sign that never-tested tree.
    11	#       Two DISTINCT failures, never merged into one message: "could not talk
